WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.279
These days, Mark Ruffalo seems to be riding
high on his blockbuster success.

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.640
But in reality, the actor has endured overwhelming
challenges to get where he is today.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.860
From life-threatening health issues, to the
loss of those closest to him, here's a look

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.000
at Mark Ruffalo's tragic real-life story.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.120
Ruffalo grew up in Wisconsin, alongside his
brother and two sisters.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.140
But according to Men's Journal, when his father,
Frank's painting business went under, the

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.830
family moved to Virginia Beach.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.110
Then, when a second business tanked, the Ruffalos
headed west.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:32.230
"Your great, great grandfather was once the
richest man in Boston."

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.940
"So how come we're so poor?"

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:39.100
In San Diego, Frank was only able to find
temporary work, and the family spiraled into

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:39.620
bankruptcy.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.540
Mark, who had just graduated high school,
has recalled in several interviews that the

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.040
family was living in a neighborhood where
drugs like meth were commonly sold.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.520
As Ruffalo recalls it, grade school was difficult.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.180
He told Parade,

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.360
"I was miserable.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.600
This sounds sappy, but I was always aware
of the frailty of human beings, the sorrow

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.640
in the nature of things.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.540
I didn't know how to live in the world, how
to cope.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.060
I felt like I didn't belong."

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:07.680
Later in life, Ruffalo discovered he had been
suffering from undiagnosed ADHD and dyslexia.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.999
In 2017, he teamed up with the Child Mind
Institute on their My Younger Self initiative,

00:01:12.999 --> 00:01:15.369
revealing a bit of his own journey with mental
health.

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:22.160
"There's help and that there are ways to deal
with it and to manage it and to overcome it."

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.180
Ruffalo even moved his young family from upstate
New York back to New York City so his children

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:30.800
could attend a school with a program for dyslexic
students, should they need it.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.340
While Ruffalo was living in L.A., he had a
best friend named Michael.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.959
The actor described their common bond, telling
Parade,

00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:40.649
"He was the only one I knew as sad as me who
I could talk to."

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:44.720
But in 1994, Michael succumbed to his own
depression, and took his own life.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.160
Ruffalo remembered,

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.500
"When he died, it rocked me out of a dark
depression.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.180
The moment he left, I realized that death
wasn't an escape."

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.920
To Ruffalo, acting became a way of moving
forward past the pain of his younger years.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.600
Ruffalo has dealt with depression for his
entire life.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.659
And according to New York Magazine, after
high school, as his friends were going to

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:08.400
college, Ruffalo said he instead spent most
of his time smoking, surfing, and wandering

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.410
around aimlessly.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.740
He worked as a busboy, and said he was,

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.120
"… just about ready to jump off a bridge.”

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.100
Ruffalo now has a name for it, telling The
Observer,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.220
"It's Dysthymia.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.790
It's a long-running, low-grade depression
all the time.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.540
I've been struggling with that my whole life."

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.680
The actor credits meditation with changing
his outlook, revealing to Rolling Stone,

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.950
"It's pretty much a daily practice that quiets
your brain and oddly enough, actually slows

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.860
down time, so you're not so much trapped in
your immediate reactions to things.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.020
My work started to change, my luck started
to change.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.720
The way the world looked to me changed."

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.120
After having a dream that he had a brain tumor,
a CAT scan confirmed Ruffalo had developed

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.140
an Acoustic Neroma, a benign tumor in his
brain.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:55.520
"She said you have a mass behind your left
ear the size of a golf ball."

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.140
It was a trying time.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.440
"Yeah it was very scary…

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.580
I found out and then our baby was born two
weeks later."

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.480
Several weeks after the birth of his son Keen,
Ruffalo underwent surgery to remove the tumor.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.010
But even though the operation was a success,
he lost hearing in his left ear, and that

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:13.280
side of his face was completely paralyzed.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.320
The crisis couldn't have come at a worse time
for Ruffalo's career, either.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:22.000
Due to the complications, he retreated to
his home where he stayed in self-imposed exile,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.000
unable to work.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.620
"It lasted a long time.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.440
It lasted to the point where they were saying
you're probably not gonna get your face back."

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:34.440
After six months of paralysis, Ruffalo beat
the odds and was able to make very slight

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.560
movements, signaling the beginning of his
recovery.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.620
According to the LA Times, Mark's brother
Scott Ruffalo died a week after being shot

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.180
in the head in his own home, in 2008.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.560
Initially it appeared that Scott might have
died playing Russian roulette, but eventually

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.160
the case was ruled a homicide.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:55.680
Police questioned Shaha Mishaal Adham and
her boyfriend Brian Scofield after they willingly

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:56.420
came forward.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:00.900
Shaha claimed she visited Scott to pick up
some keys, said Scott then mentioned something

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.740
about Russian roulette, and Shaha says she
heard a gunshot shortly after.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:10.080
She was booked, but then released, and in
2012, she suddenly died, leaving the case

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.560
without a critical witness.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.720
Scott's murder remains unsolved.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.600
"You know it's, it'll be the great mystery
of my life."

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.360
Following his brother's death, Ruffalo took
a break from Hollywood.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.620
He told the Telegraph,

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.819
"My brother passing away… reminded me that
life is short and you'd better do what you

00:04:26.819 --> 00:04:28.249
want while you have a chance."

00:04:28.249 --> 00:04:32.979
Ruffalo fired his agent and publicist, left
his apartment in L.A., and moved to a secluded

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.340
home in upstate New York with his wife and
three children.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.580
Still, Ruffalo couldn't completely leave the
business, and went on to make his directorial

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.300
debut with 2010's Sympathy for Delicious.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.800
Ruffalo remained semi-retired from acting
until he read the script for The Kids Are

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:46.380
All Right.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:50.280
As he told the Telegraph, he took on the project
in memory of his brother.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:58.680
"He was this incredibly beautiful, sexy, vibrant,
fun loving guy…

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:04.120
It was a way for me to say thank you to him."

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:09.260
The actor has since gone on to enviable success,
despite the many devastating challenges he's

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.200
faced in his life.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.140
He looked back on his struggle, telling Life&amp;Style,

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.380
"I was tending bar at Chateau Marmont, and
I’d see Johnny Depp and Nic Cage hanging

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:20.740
around, hugely successful, while I was barely
making a living…

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.880
I must have auditioned 800 times without landing
a part."

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:28.060
Thanks to the support of his wife and three
children, and a whole lot of honest work on

00:05:28.069 --> 00:05:32.470
his well-being, the guy now widely known as
Hulk from The Avengers is living his best

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:32.960
life.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:41.080
"Just be patient, and accept the journey that
you've been asked to take."

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:45.780
If you or anyone you know is having suicidal
thoughts, please call the National Suicide

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:49.400
Prevention Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (8255).

